// The Stonemason's stock in western Keldagrim.
//
// Four things, at OSRS's own quantities and its one-minute restock: a thousand limestone bricks,
// twenty marble blocks, twenty gold leaves and ten magic stones.
//
// The PRICES are not here. ^poh_stone_sell is 1300 and a shop charges cost x multiplier / 1000, so
// each comes out at 130% of the item's value - 26 for a limestone brick, 325,000 for a marble
// block, 130,000 for gold leaf, 975,000 for a magic stone. Those are his four rows in the live
// game. He buys back at 50%: 10, 125,000, 50,000, 375,000.
//
// HE SOLD AT HIS BUYING PRICE UNTIL 2026-09-15. ^poh_stone_sell was 500, which is the ratio he buys
// at, and the costs had been inflated to compensate - so a marble block was 125,000 instead of
// 325,000 and a brick was 10 instead of 26. Gold leaf came out right by coincidence and that is
// probably why it stood for so long. The magic stone was worse: it arrived with the costume room's
// cape rack at an invented 4,000,000, four times what he charges, asserted in three places and
// checked against itself. Read the shop row.

[poh_stone_shop]
scope=shared
size=40
restock=yes
allstock=no
stackall=no
stock1=limestonebrick,1000,100
stock2=poh_marble_block,20,100
stock3=gold_leaf,20,100
stock4=magic_stone,10,100
